From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:46:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 91/91] web-app: re-check unread messages in view when the tab
 becomes visible

The unread-message IntersectionObserver callback drops its entries
while the document has no focus, and only a window 'focus' event
re-observes them. When a tab or installed PWA comes back to the
foreground, the observer delivers its pending entries in the first
frame, which can be before the document has focus again; mobile
browsers (iOS Safari standalone especially) may not fire 'focus' on
resume at all. The message was then on screen but stayed unread until
the chat was re-entered. Re-observe on 'visibilitychange' as well.
---
 .../src/components/message/MessageList.tsx         | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/message/MessageList.tsx b/packages/frontend/src/components/message/MessageList.tsx
index 7c3f8ca..8004bc8 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/message/MessageList.tsx
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/message/MessageList.tsx
@@ -216,9 +216,21 @@ export default function MessageList({
   }, [unreadMessageInViewIntersectionObserver])
 
   useEffect(() => {
+    // Also on `visibilitychange`: when a tab or PWA comes back, the observer
+    // delivers its pending entries in the first frame, often before the
+    // document has focus again, and mobile browsers may never fire `focus`.
     window.addEventListener('focus', reInvokeAllUnreadObservations)
-    return () =>
+    document.addEventListener(
+      'visibilitychange',
+      reInvokeAllUnreadObservations
+    )
+    return () => {
       window.removeEventListener('focus', reInvokeAllUnreadObservations)
+      document.removeEventListener(
+        'visibilitychange',
+        reInvokeAllUnreadObservations
+      )
+    }
   }, [reInvokeAllUnreadObservations])
 
   useEffect(() => {
